@startuml Login and Attribution

title Linking a login to a person, and attributing every change
caption Target design. Decisions O34, O35, O19. ADR 0017. Plans 02 and 03.

autonumber

actor Administrator as admin
actor "Volunteer\n(any role)" as vol
participant "Identity provider\n(Entra / Keycloak)" as idp
participant "Freedom web" as web
participant "Freedom API" as api
database "dbo.PersonDetail\n(erasable)" as detail
database "Entity tables" as tables

== A volunteer signs in for the first time ==
vol -> idp : sign in
idp --> vol : token (subject, roles)
vol -> web : open Freedom
web -> api : GET /me
api -> detail : find person by IdentitySubject
detail --> api : none
api --> web : subject and roles, **not linked**
note right of web
  A login that is not linked can read what its roles allow,
  but cannot make any change that records who did it.
end note

== The Administrator links the login ==
admin -> web : open the volunteer's person record
web -> api : PUT /people/{id}/login { subject }
api -> detail : set IdentitySubject (unique)
alt subject already linked to someone else
  detail --> api : conflict
  api --> web : 409
else linked
  detail --> api : ok
  api --> web : 204
end

== Every change records who made it ==
vol -> web : change something (for example validate a box)
web -> api : write request (no person id in the body)
api -> detail : resolve caller's person from the token subject
alt not linked, or erased
  api --> web : **403 login-not-linked**
  note right : No "unknown" identity is ever written (O35)
else linked
  api -> tables : UPDATE ... , LastChangedBy = person, LastChangedAt = now\n(same statement as the change)
  tables --> api : ok
  api --> web : 200
end

== Erasure removes the link with the personal data ==
admin -> api : DELETE /people/{id}
api -> detail : delete PersonDetail (subject goes with it)
api -> tables : identity kept only if a record names it
note over tables
  Records that name an erased person read "Former volunteer".
end note

@enduml
